IMPORT prelude

-- Trade Marks Act 1995 (Cth) -- the questions of the trade mark applicant and registered owner.
--
-- SEAT: the founder, applying for and then owning a registered trade mark through the company (in the WA lives, Daniel for
-- Jarrah Legal Technologies Pty Ltd and its JARRAH mark): "Can my sign be registered?", "Must my application be rejected?",
-- "When does my registration start and end, and how do I renew it?", "Is the copy an infringement?", "Is my letter safe?",
-- "Can my mark be taken off the Register for non-use?", "May I mark it as registered?".
--
-- Provisions covered: periods in months (s 6A); "sign" (s 6); what a trade mark is (s 17); who may apply (s 27(1), (2)(c));
-- grounds for rejection (ss 39(1), 40, 41, 42, 43, 44); acceptance, a hearing before rejection, and appeal (ss 33, 35); date
-- and term of registration (s 72); which renewal Division applies (s 74A, s 80A(1)); renewal and failure to renew (ss 75, 77,
-- 78, 79); the exclusive rights (s 20); infringement (s 120(1)-(3)); when there is no infringement (ss 122(1), (2), 124);
-- relief and its limits (ss 126, 127, 128(1)); unjustified threats and mere notification (ss 129, 130A); removal for non-use
-- (ss 92(4), 93, 100(3)(c), 101(3)); false representation that a mark is registered (s 151(1), (3), (5)).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 48, compilation date 19 September 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 87, 2026), register id
-- C2026C00421, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A04969.txt (retrieved 13 October 2026). The Trade Marks
-- Regulations 1995 are NOT deposited: the prescribed period before expiry within which renewal may be asked (s 75(1)), the
-- signs the regulations forbid (s 39(1)), the classes (s 19(3)) and all fees (s 223) are INPUTS or left out. The dollar value
-- of a penalty unit (Crimes Act 1914, not deposited) is not used.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: application procedure, publication, examination reports, deferment, lapsing (ss 27(2)-(5), 28-32, 34, 36-38);
-- divisional and series applications (ss 45-51A); opposition (Part 5) beyond noting it; amendment and rectification (Parts 6,
-- 8); Division 3 renewal for registrations entered 10 or more years after filing (ss 80A-80H: the encoding says when it
-- applies, and stops); assignment and interests (Parts 10, 11); s 121 (notices of prohibition); s 122A (exhaustion); s 123;
-- import seizure (Part 13); offences other than s 151 (Part 14); collective, certification and defensive marks (Parts 15-17);
-- the Madrid Protocol (Part 17A); courts, the Registrar, attorneys, and the transitional Part 21 (machinery or not met by the
-- seat); s 223A (office closed on the last day) and s 224 (extensions of time).
--
-- Dates are written YYYYMMDD as numbers. 0 means "no such date".
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the seat of the trade mark applicant and owner, with the
-- design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public
-- use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Trade Marks Act 1995 -- the applicant and registered owner`

§§ `s 6A -- periods expressed in months`

-- s 6A: "a period expressed in months and dating from an event ends: (a) on the day, in the relevant subsequent month, which
-- has the same number as the day of the event; or (b) if the relevant subsequent month has no day with the same number--on the
-- last day of the month."
-- INFERENCE: the 10-year periods of ss 72(3), 77 and 79 are read as 120 months under the same rule, so that 10 years from
-- 29 February ends on 28 February.

GIVEN `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a leap year` MEANS
        (`y` MODULO 4 EQUALS 0 AND (NOT (`y` MODULO 100 EQUALS 0)))
    OR  `y` MODULO 400 EQUALS 0

GIVEN `y` IS A NUMBER
      `m` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days in month` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `m` EQUALS 2 THEN IF `is a leap year` `y` THEN 29 ELSE 28
           IF `m` EQUALS 4 OR `m` EQUALS 6 OR `m` EQUALS 9 OR `m` EQUALS 11 THEN 30
           OTHERWISE 31

@export On what day does a period of so many months from this date end (s 6A)?
GIVEN `the date` IS A NUMBER @desc The date of the event, written YYYYMMDD
      `months` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of months in the period
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the day a period of months ends` IS
    `new year` TIMES 10000 PLUS `new month` TIMES 100 PLUS `new day`
    WHERE
        `y` MEANS TRUNC (`the date` / 10000) 0
        `m` MEANS TRUNC ((`the date` MODULO 10000) / 100) 0
        `d` MEANS `the date` MODULO 100
        `count` MEANS `y` TIMES 12 PLUS (`m` MINUS 1) PLUS `months`
        `new year` MEANS TRUNC (`count` / 12) 0
        `new month` MEANS (`count` MODULO 12) PLUS 1
        `new day` MEANS IF `d` GREATER THAN `days in month` `new year` `new month`
                        THEN `days in month` `new year` `new month`
                        ELSE `d`

§§ `ss 6, 17 -- what a trade mark is`

-- s 6: "sign includes the following or any combination of the following, namely, any letter, word, name, signature, numeral,
-- device, brand, heading, label, ticket, aspect of packaging, shape, colour, sound or scent."
-- s 17: "A trade mark is a sign used, or intended to be used, to distinguish goods or services dealt with or provided in the
-- course of trade by a person from goods or services so dealt with or provided by any other person."

-- SignKind: what the sign is. The s 6 list is inclusive ("includes"), so anything else is asked as a fact.
DECLARE SignKind IS ONE OF
    `a letter`
    `a word`
    `a name`
    `a signature`
    `a numeral`
    `a device`
    `a brand`
    `a heading`
    `a label`
    `a ticket`
    `an aspect of packaging`
    `a shape`
    `a colour`
    `a sound`
    `a scent`
    `a combination of these`
    `something else`

-- Adaptation: how far the sign is inherently adapted to distinguish my goods or services (s 41(3)(a), (4)(a)). This is the
-- Registrar's assessment, so it is an input.
DECLARE Adaptation IS ONE OF
    `not to any extent`
    `to some extent but not sufficiently`
    `sufficiently`

-- Mark: the facts about my sign and what I want it registered for.
DECLARE Mark HAS
    `what kind of sign it is` IS A SignKind
    `it is otherwise a sign` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I use or intend to use it to distinguish my goods or services in trade` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it can be represented graphically` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it contains a sign the regulations forbid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `how far it is inherently adapted to distinguish` IS AN Adaptation
    `I used it before filing so much that it in fact distinguishes my goods or services` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Registrar finds it does or will distinguish them on the combined effect in s 41(4)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it contains scandalous matter` IS A BOOLEAN
    `its use would be contrary to law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a connotation it has makes its use for my goods or services likely to deceive or confuse` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Is my sign a "sign" (s 6)?
GIVEN `the mark` IS A Mark @desc Your sign and what you want it registered for
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it a sign` IF
    CONSIDER `the mark`'s `what kind of sign it is`
    WHEN `something else` THEN `the mark`'s `it is otherwise a sign`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

@export Is my sign a trade mark (s 17)?
GIVEN `the mark` IS A Mark @desc Your sign and what you want it registered for
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my sign a trade mark` IF
        `Is it a sign` `the mark`
    AND `the mark`'s `I use or intend to use it to distinguish my goods or services in trade`

§§ `s 27 -- who may apply`

-- s 27(1): "A person may apply for the registration of a trade mark in respect of goods and/or services if: (a) the person
-- claims to be the owner of the trade mark; and (b) one of the following applies: (i) the person is using or intends to use
-- the trade mark ...; (ii) the person has authorised or intends to authorise another person to use the trade mark ...; (iii)
-- the person intends to assign the trade mark to a body corporate that is about to be constituted ...".
-- s 27(2)(c): the application must "be made by a person or persons having legal personality".

-- UseBasis: the s 27(1)(b) limb I rely on.
DECLARE UseBasis IS ONE OF
    `I use or intend to use it`
    `I have authorised or intend to authorise another to use it`
    `I intend to assign it to a body corporate about to be constituted, for its use`
    `none of these`

DECLARE Applicant HAS
    `I claim to be the owner of the trade mark` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my basis for use` IS A UseBasis
    `I have legal personality` IS A BOOLEAN

@export May I apply to register the trade mark (s 27(1), (2)(c))?
GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant @desc Who is applying, and on what basis
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply` IF
        `me`'s `I claim to be the owner of the trade mark`
    AND (NOT (`me`'s `my basis for use` EQUALS `none of these`))
    AND `me`'s `I have legal personality`

§§ `ss 39-44 -- grounds for rejecting my application`

-- s 39(1): rejected "if the trade mark contains or consists of a sign that, under regulations made for the purposes of section
-- 18, is not to be used as a trade mark". s 40: rejected "if the trade mark cannot be represented graphically".
-- s 41(1): rejected "if the trade mark is not capable of distinguishing the applicant's goods or services"; (2) only if (3) or
-- (4) applies; (3) "not to any extent inherently adapted to distinguish" and not used before filing "to such an extent that
-- the trade mark does in fact distinguish"; (4) "to some extent, but not sufficiently, inherently adapted" and "does not and
-- will not distinguish" on the combined effect of adaptation, use or intended use, and other circumstances.
-- s 42: rejected if "(a) the trade mark contains or consists of scandalous matter; or (b) its use would be contrary to law".
-- s 43: rejected if "because of some connotation ... the use of the trade mark in relation to those goods or services would be
-- likely to deceive or cause confusion".

@export Is my trade mark capable of distinguishing my goods or services (s 41)?
GIVEN `the mark` IS A Mark @desc Your sign and what you want it registered for
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my mark capable of distinguishing` IF
    CONSIDER `the mark`'s `how far it is inherently adapted to distinguish`
    WHEN `not to any extent` THEN `the mark`'s `I used it before filing so much that it in fact distinguishes my goods or services`
    WHEN `to some extent but not sufficiently` THEN `the mark`'s `the Registrar finds it does or will distinguish them on the combined effect in s 41(4)(b)`
    WHEN `sufficiently` THEN TRUE

-- s 44(1), (2): rejected if my mark "is substantially identical with, or deceptively similar to" another person's mark
-- registered or sought for similar goods or closely related services (or similar services or closely related goods), and "the
-- priority date for the registration of the applicant's trade mark ... is not earlier than the priority date" of the other.
-- s 12: the priority date is the date of registration, which s 72 makes the filing date (or a Convention date).
-- s 44(3): if the Registrar is satisfied of "honest concurrent use" or that "because of other circumstances, it is proper to
-- do so", the Registrar "may accept the application ... subject to any conditions or limitations".
-- s 44(4): if the Registrar is satisfied I "continuously used" my mark from before the other's priority date to mine, "the
-- Registrar may not reject the application because of the existence of the other trade mark".

-- Rival: another person's mark already registered or sought, as it bears on s 44. "Deceptively similar" (s 10) and
-- "similar goods" (s 14) are applied by the Registrar, so they are inputs.
DECLARE Rival HAS
    `there is such a mark` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my mark is substantially identical with or deceptively similar to it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is for similar or closely related goods or services` IS A BOOLEAN
    `its priority date` IS A NUMBER
    `the Registrar is satisfied I used mine continuously from before its priority date to mine` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Registrar is satisfied of honest concurrent use or other circumstances making acceptance proper` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `my priority date` IS A NUMBER @desc Your priority date (your filing date, or Convention date), YYYYMMDD
      `the rival` IS A Rival @desc Another person's earlier mark, if any
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my mark conflicts under s 44(1) or (2)` IF
        `the rival`'s `there is such a mark`
    AND `the rival`'s `my mark is substantially identical with or deceptively similar to it`
    AND `the rival`'s `it is for similar or closely related goods or services`
    AND `my priority date` AT LEAST `the rival`'s `its priority date`
    AND (NOT `the rival`'s `the Registrar is satisfied I used mine continuously from before its priority date to mine`)

-- Examination: what happens to my application, as I would want it told to me.
DECLARE Examination IS ONE OF
    `not a trade mark at all (s 17)`
    `I may not apply (s 27)`
    `must be rejected: a sign the regulations forbid (s 39(1))`
    `must be rejected: cannot be represented graphically (s 40)`
    `must be rejected: not capable of distinguishing (s 41)`
    `must be rejected: scandalous or its use contrary to law (s 42)`
    `must be rejected: likely to deceive or cause confusion (s 43)`
    `may be accepted with conditions or limitations, the Registrar being satisfied under s 44(3)`
    `must be rejected: conflicts with an earlier mark (s 44)`
    `must be accepted, though possibly with conditions or limitations (s 33(1), (2))`

-- s 33(1): "The Registrar must, after the examination, accept the application unless he or she is satisfied that ... there are
-- grounds under this Act for rejecting it." The grounds are tested in the order of the Act.
@export Will my application be accepted or must it be rejected (ss 17, 27, 33, 39-44)?
GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant @desc Who is applying, and on what basis
      `the mark` IS A Mark @desc Your sign and what you want it registered for
      `my priority date` IS A NUMBER @desc Your filing date (or Convention date), YYYYMMDD
      `the rival` IS A Rival @desc Another person's earlier mark, if any
GIVETH AN Examination
DECIDE `Will my application be accepted` IS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `Is my sign a trade mark` `the mark`) THEN `not a trade mark at all (s 17)`
           IF (NOT `May I apply` `me`) THEN `I may not apply (s 27)`
           IF `the mark`'s `it contains a sign the regulations forbid` THEN `must be rejected: a sign the regulations forbid (s 39(1))`
           IF (NOT `the mark`'s `it can be represented graphically`) THEN `must be rejected: cannot be represented graphically (s 40)`
           IF (NOT `Is my mark capable of distinguishing` `the mark`) THEN `must be rejected: not capable of distinguishing (s 41)`
           IF     `the mark`'s `it contains scandalous matter`
               OR `the mark`'s `its use would be contrary to law` THEN `must be rejected: scandalous or its use contrary to law (s 42)`
           IF `the mark`'s `a connotation it has makes its use for my goods or services likely to deceive or confuse`
              THEN `must be rejected: likely to deceive or cause confusion (s 43)`
           IF `my mark conflicts under s 44(1) or (2)` `my priority date` `the rival`
              THEN IF `the rival`'s `the Registrar is satisfied of honest concurrent use or other circumstances making acceptance proper`
                   THEN `may be accepted with conditions or limitations, the Registrar being satisfied under s 44(3)`
                   ELSE `must be rejected: conflicts with an earlier mark (s 44)`
           OTHERWISE `must be accepted, though possibly with conditions or limitations (s 33(1), (2))`

-- s 33(4): "The Registrar may not reject an application without giving the applicant an opportunity of being heard."
-- s 35: "The applicant may appeal to the Federal Court or the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2)
-- against a decision of the Registrar: (a) to accept the application subject to conditions or limitations; or (b) to reject
-- the application."
@export Must I be heard first, and may I appeal to the Federal Court or the FCFCOA (ss 33(4), 35)?
GIVEN `the outcome` IS AN Examination @desc The outcome of examination
      `accepted subject to conditions or limitations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an acceptance came with conditions or limitations
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I appeal` IF
    CONSIDER `the outcome`
    WHEN `must be accepted, though possibly with conditions or limitations (s 33(1), (2))` THEN `accepted subject to conditions or limitations`
    WHEN `may be accepted with conditions or limitations, the Registrar being satisfied under s 44(3)` THEN `accepted subject to conditions or limitations`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

@export Must the Registrar give me a hearing before rejecting my application (s 33(4))?
GIVEN `the outcome` IS AN Examination @desc The outcome of examination
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be heard before rejection` IF
    CONSIDER `the outcome`
    WHEN `must be accepted, though possibly with conditions or limitations (s 33(1), (2))` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `may be accepted with conditions or limitations, the Registrar being satisfied under s 44(3)` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `s 72 -- date and term of registration`

-- s 72(1): the registration "is taken to have had effect from (and including) the filing date in respect of the application".
-- s 72(2): if I claimed Convention priority under s 29, from the day of the (earliest) Convention application.
-- s 72(3): "Unless it is earlier cancelled, or the trade mark is earlier removed from the Register, the registration of the
-- trade mark expires 10 years after the filing date" -- Note 1: "This is so even for" a Convention-dated registration.
-- s 77(1): on renewal before expiry, "for a period of 10 years from the day on which the registration of the trade mark would
-- expire if it were not renewed". s 79: on renewal within 6 months after expiry, "for 10 years from the day on which the
-- registration expired".

-- Registration: the facts of my registration, from the Register and my own records.
DECLARE Registration HAS
    `filing date` IS A NUMBER
    `Convention application date` IS A NUMBER
    `date particulars were entered in the Register` IS A NUMBER
    `renewals so far` IS A NUMBER
    `date of my late renewal under s 79` IS A NUMBER
    `date I first used the mark` IS A NUMBER

@export From what day does my registration take effect (s 72(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my registration` IS A Registration @desc Your registration
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `When does my registration take effect` IS
    IF `my registration`'s `Convention application date` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `my registration`'s `Convention application date`
    ELSE `my registration`'s `filing date`

@export On what day does my registration first expire (s 72(3))?
GIVEN `my registration` IS A Registration @desc Your registration
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `When does my registration first expire` IS
    `the day a period of months ends` (`my registration`'s `filing date`) 120

-- Each renewal, early (s 77) or late (s 79), runs 10 years from the day the registration expired or would have expired.
@export On what day does my registration now expire, counting the renewals made (ss 72(3), 77, 79)?
GIVEN `my registration` IS A Registration @desc Your registration
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `When does my registration now expire` IS
    `the day a period of months ends` (`my registration`'s `filing date`) (120 TIMES (1 PLUS `my registration`'s `renewals so far`))

-- INFERENCE: "expires 10 years after the filing date" is read as: in force on every day before the expiry day, and not on it.
@export Is my registration in force on this day (ss 72, 77-79)?
GIVEN `my registration` IS A Registration @desc Your registration
      `the day` IS A NUMBER @desc The day asked about, YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my registration in force on` IF
        `my registration`'s `date particulars were entered in the Register` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the day` AT LEAST `When does my registration take effect` `my registration`
    AND `the day` LESS THAN `When does my registration now expire` `my registration`

§§ `ss 74A, 80A -- which renewal Division applies`

-- s 74A: Division 2 applies if "particulars of registration were entered in the Register under section 69 before the end of
-- the period of 10 years after the filing date". s 80A(1): Division 3 applies if they were entered after the end of that period.
DECLARE RenewalDivision IS ONE OF
    `Division 2 of Part 7 (ss 75-80)`
    `Division 3 of Part 7 (ss 80A-80H), which this encoding does not cover`
    `neither: the mark is not yet registered`

@export Which renewal rules apply to my registration (ss 74A, 80A)?
GIVEN `my registration` IS A Registration @desc Your registration
GIVETH A RenewalDivision
DECIDE `Which renewal rules apply to me` IS
    BRANCH IF `my registration`'s `date particulars were entered in the Register` EQUALS 0 THEN `neither: the mark is not yet registered`
           IF `my registration`'s `date particulars were entered in the Register` LESS THAN `When does my registration first expire` `my registration`
              THEN `Division 2 of Part 7 (ss 75-80)`
           OTHERWISE `Division 3 of Part 7 (ss 80A-80H), which this encoding does not cover`

§§ `ss 75-79 -- renewal`

-- s 75(1): "Any person may, within the prescribed period before the registration of a trade mark expires, ask the Registrar to
-- renew the registration." The prescribed period is set by the Trade Marks Regulations 1995, not deposited: an INPUT in months.
-- s 77(1): the Registrar "must renew the registration for a period of 10 years from the day on which the registration of the
-- trade mark would expire". s 78: if not renewed, "(a) subject to sections 79 and 80, the registration ceases to have effect
-- when it expires; and (b) unless the registration is renewed under section 79, the Registrar must remove the trade mark from
-- the Register 6 months after the day on which the registration expired." s 79: a request "within 6 months after the
-- registration of a trade mark has expired" -- the Registrar "must renew ... for 10 years from the day on which the
-- registration expired". s 128(1): after a s 79 renewal, no action "in respect of an act that ... infringed the trade mark;
-- and ... was done after the registration had expired and before it was renewed".

DECLARE RenewalOutcome IS ONE OF
    `too early: not yet within the prescribed period before expiry (s 75(1))`
    `renewed for 10 years from the day it would have expired (s 77)`
    `renewed late for 10 years from the day it expired, with no action for acts in the gap (ss 79, 128(1))`
    `too late: the mark is removed 6 months after expiry (s 78(b))`
    `Division 3 applies or the mark is not registered: not covered here`

@export If I ask to renew on this day, what happens (ss 75, 77, 78, 79)?
GIVEN `my registration` IS A Registration @desc Your registration
      `the day I ask` IS A NUMBER @desc The day you file the renewal request, YYYYMMDD
      `prescribed months before expiry` IS A NUMBER @desc The prescribed period before expiry, in months, set by the Trade Marks Regulations (an input)
GIVETH A RenewalOutcome
DECIDE `What happens if I ask to renew on` IS
    BRANCH IF (NOT (`Which renewal rules apply to me` `my registration` EQUALS `Division 2 of Part 7 (ss 75-80)`))
              THEN `Division 3 applies or the mark is not registered: not covered here`
           IF `the day a period of months ends` `the day I ask` `prescribed months before expiry` LESS THAN `the expiry`
              THEN `too early: not yet within the prescribed period before expiry (s 75(1))`
           IF `the day I ask` LESS THAN `the expiry` THEN `renewed for 10 years from the day it would have expired (s 77)`
           IF `the day I ask` AT MOST `By when can I still renew late` `my registration`
              THEN `renewed late for 10 years from the day it expired, with no action for acts in the gap (ss 79, 128(1))`
           OTHERWISE `too late: the mark is removed 6 months after expiry (s 78(b))`
    WHERE
        `the expiry` MEANS `When does my registration now expire` `my registration`

-- INFERENCE: "within 6 months after" is read as including the day on which the 6 months end under s 6A.
@export What is the last day on which I can still renew late (s 79)?
GIVEN `my registration` IS A Registration @desc Your registration
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `By when can I still renew late` IS
    `the day a period of months ends` (`When does my registration now expire` `my registration`) 6

@export If renewed now, until when would my registration run (ss 77, 79)?
GIVEN `my registration` IS A Registration @desc Your registration
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Until when would renewal carry my registration` IS
    `the day a period of months ends` (`When does my registration now expire` `my registration`) 120

§§ `s 20 -- my exclusive rights`

-- s 20(1): "the registered owner of the trade mark has, subject to this Part, the exclusive rights: (a) to use the trade mark;
-- and (b) to authorise other persons to use the trade mark; in relation to the goods and/or services in respect of which the
-- trade mark is registered." (2): "also the right to obtain relief under this Act if the trade mark has been infringed."
-- (3): "The rights are taken to have accrued to the registered owner as from the date of registration of the trade mark."
@export Do I have the exclusive right to use, and to authorise others to use, my mark on this day (s 20)?
GIVEN `my registration` IS A Registration @desc Your registration
      `the day` IS A NUMBER @desc The day asked about, YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have the exclusive rights on` IF
    `Is my registration in force on` `my registration` `the day`

§§ `s 120 -- infringement`

-- s 120(1): "A person infringes a registered trade mark if the person uses as a trade mark a sign that is substantially
-- identical with, or deceptively similar to, the trade mark in relation to goods or services in respect of which the trade
-- mark is registered."
-- s 120(2): the same for goods or services "of the same description" or "closely related"; "However, the person is not taken to
-- have infringed the trade mark if the person establishes that using the sign as the person did is not likely to deceive or
-- cause confusion."
-- s 120(3): for unrelated goods or services, if "(a) the trade mark is well known in Australia", "(c) because the trade mark is
-- well known, the sign would be likely to be taken as indicating a connection ... and (d) for that reason, the interests of
-- the registered owner are likely to be adversely affected."
-- s 10: "deceptively similar" -- "so nearly resembles that other trade mark that it is likely to deceive or cause confusion".
-- That is the court's judgment, so it is an input.

-- Closeness: how near the other sign comes to my mark.
DECLARE Closeness IS ONE OF
    `substantially identical`
    `deceptively similar`
    `neither`

-- Field: what the other person uses the sign on, measured against my registration.
DECLARE Field IS ONE OF
    `the goods or services my mark is registered for`
    `goods or services of the same description, or closely related`
    `unrelated goods or services`

-- Defence: the s 122 answer the other person may have.
DECLARE Defence IS ONE OF
    `none`
    `their own name or place of business, in good faith (s 122(1)(a))`
    `a sign indicating a characteristic of the goods or services, in good faith (s 122(1)(b))`
    `my mark used in good faith to indicate intended purpose (s 122(1)(c))`
    `comparative advertising (s 122(1)(d))`
    `exercising a right to use a trade mark given under this Act (s 122(1)(e))`
    `the court thinks they would obtain registration of it (s 122(1)(f), (fa))`
    `outside a condition or limitation on my registration (s 122(1)(g))`
    `using only a disclaimed part of my mark (s 122(2))`

-- OtherUse: one use by another person -- the natural unit is one sign used on one line of goods or services.
DECLARE OtherUse HAS
    `the day of the use` IS A NUMBER
    `they use the sign as a trade mark` IS A BOOLEAN
    `how close their sign is` IS A Closeness
    `what they use it on` IS A Field
    `they establish their use is not likely to deceive or cause confusion` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my mark is well known in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it would suggest a connection with me that is likely to harm my interests` IS A BOOLEAN
    `their defence` IS A Defence
    `the day their continuous use of an unregistered mark began` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE Infringement IS ONE OF
    `infringes: same goods or services (s 120(1))`
    `infringes: goods or services of the same description or closely related (s 120(2))`
    `infringes: a well-known mark on unrelated goods or services (s 120(3))`
    `no infringement: my registration was not in force that day`
    `no infringement: they do not use the sign as a trade mark`
    `no infringement: their sign is not substantially identical or deceptively similar`
    `no infringement: they establish no likelihood of deception or confusion (s 120(2))`
    `no infringement: the s 120(3) conditions are not met`
    `no infringement: a s 122 defence applies`
    `no infringement: their continuous prior use (s 124)`

-- s 124(1): no infringement by an unregistered mark used continuously "from a time before: (e) the date of registration of the
-- registered trade mark; or (f) the registered owner ... first used the trade mark; whichever is earlier." It reaches similar
-- or closely related goods and services (s 124(1)(a)-(d)); s 14 makes the same goods "similar". (2): the defence is limited to
-- the area of use (not encoded; the case is one area).
GIVEN `my registration` IS A Registration @desc Your registration
      `the use` IS AN OtherUse @desc The other person's use
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `they have prior continuous use under s 124` IF
        `the use`'s `the day their continuous use of an unregistered mark began` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the use`'s `the day their continuous use of an unregistered mark began` LESS THAN `the earlier date`
    AND (NOT (`the use`'s `what they use it on` EQUALS `unrelated goods or services`))
    WHERE
        `the registration date` MEANS `When does my registration take effect` `my registration`
        `first use` MEANS `my registration`'s `date I first used the mark`
        `the earlier date` MEANS IF `first use` GREATER THAN 0 AND `first use` LESS THAN `the registration date`
                                 THEN `first use`
                                 ELSE `the registration date`

@export Is the copy an infringement of my registered trade mark (ss 120, 122, 124)?
GIVEN `my registration` IS A Registration @desc Your registration
      `the use` IS AN OtherUse @desc The other person's use of a sign like yours
GIVETH AN Infringement
DECIDE `Is the copy an infringement` IS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `Is my registration in force on` `my registration` (`the use`'s `the day of the use`))
              THEN `no infringement: my registration was not in force that day`
           IF (NOT `the use`'s `they use the sign as a trade mark`) THEN `no infringement: they do not use the sign as a trade mark`
           IF `the use`'s `how close their sign is` EQUALS `neither`
              THEN `no infringement: their sign is not substantially identical or deceptively similar`
           IF (NOT (`the use`'s `their defence` EQUALS `none`)) THEN `no infringement: a s 122 defence applies`
           IF `they have prior continuous use under s 124` `my registration` `the use` THEN `no infringement: their continuous prior use (s 124)`
           OTHERWISE CONSIDER `the use`'s `what they use it on`
                     WHEN `the goods or services my mark is registered for` THEN `infringes: same goods or services (s 120(1))`
                     WHEN `goods or services of the same description, or closely related` THEN
                          IF `the use`'s `they establish their use is not likely to deceive or cause confusion`
                          THEN `no infringement: they establish no likelihood of deception or confusion (s 120(2))`
                          ELSE `infringes: goods or services of the same description or closely related (s 120(2))`
                     WHEN `unrelated goods or services` THEN
                          IF     `the use`'s `my mark is well known in Australia`
                             AND `the use`'s `it would suggest a connection with me that is likely to harm my interests`
                          THEN `infringes: a well-known mark on unrelated goods or services (s 120(3))`
                          ELSE `no infringement: the s 120(3) conditions are not met`

GIVEN `outcome` IS AN Infringement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is an infringement` MEANS
       `outcome` EQUALS `infringes: same goods or services (s 120(1))`
    OR `outcome` EQUALS `infringes: goods or services of the same description or closely related (s 120(2))`
    OR `outcome` EQUALS `infringes: a well-known mark on unrelated goods or services (s 120(3))`

§§ `ss 126-128 -- what I can get from the court`

-- s 126(1): relief "includes: (a) an injunction ...; and (b) at the option of the plaintiff but subject to section 127, damages
-- or an account of profits." (2): an additional amount for flagrancy and other listed matters.
-- s 127: no damages or account of profits "in respect of any infringement of the trade mark that happened during the critical
-- period" if the defendant has sought removal under s 92 and the court finds non-use grounds for that period.
-- s 128(1): see above (the gap before a s 79 renewal).

@export Can I bring an action for this infringement at all (ss 120, 128(1))?
GIVEN `my registration` IS A Registration @desc Your registration
      `the use` IS AN OtherUse @desc The other person's use
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I sue for this use` IF
        `is an infringement` (`Is the copy an infringement` `my registration` `the use`)
    AND (NOT `the use falls in the s 128 gap`)
    WHERE
        `late renewal` MEANS `my registration`'s `date of my late renewal under s 79`
        `expired on` MEANS `the day a period of months ends` (`my registration`'s `filing date`) (120 TIMES `my registration`'s `renewals so far`)
        `the use falls in the s 128 gap` MEANS
                `late renewal` GREATER THAN 0
            AND `the use`'s `the day of the use` AT LEAST `expired on`
            AND `the use`'s `the day of the use` LESS THAN `late renewal`

-- INFERENCE (s 128(1) and s 78(a)): an act in the gap is treated as within the registration once it is renewed late, so that
-- s 128 is what bars the action; `Is the copy an infringement` therefore counts the late renewal in `renewals so far`.

@export Can I get damages or an account of profits, not only an injunction (ss 126, 127)?
GIVEN `my registration` IS A Registration @desc Your registration
      `the use` IS AN OtherUse @desc The other person's use
      `they sought removal for non-use and the court found grounds covering the time of the use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether s 127 applies
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I get damages or an account of profits` IF
        `Can I sue for this use` `my registration` `the use`
    AND (NOT `they sought removal for non-use and the court found grounds covering the time of the use`)

§§ `ss 129, 130A -- my letter`

-- s 129(1): if a person threatens to bring an action for infringement, "any person aggrieved by the threat" may sue for a
-- declaration, an injunction and damages. (4): "The court may not find in favour of the plaintiff if the defendant satisfies
-- the court that: (a) the trade mark is registered; and (b) the acts of the threatened person ... constitute an infringement".
-- s 130A: "The mere notification of the existence of a registered trade mark does not constitute a threat to bring an action".

DECLARE Letter IS ONE OF
    `a mere notification that my trade mark is registered`
    `a threat to sue for infringement`

@export Is my letter safe from an action for unjustified threats (ss 129, 130A)?
GIVEN `my registration` IS A Registration @desc Your registration
      `the letter` IS A Letter @desc What your letter does
      `the use` IS AN OtherUse @desc The use your letter complains of
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my letter safe from an unjustified threats claim` IF
    CONSIDER `the letter`
    WHEN `a mere notification that my trade mark is registered` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a threat to sue for infringement` THEN `is an infringement` (`Is the copy an infringement` `my registration` `the use`)

§§ `ss 92, 93, 100, 101 -- removal for non-use`

-- s 92(4)(a): at filing I "had no intention in good faith" to use, authorise use or assign for use in Australia, and I have not
-- used it (in good faith) in Australia "at any time before the period of one month ending on the day on which the non-use
-- application is filed". s 93(1): that ground "may be made at any time after the filing date".
-- s 92(4)(b): "the trade mark has remained registered for a continuous period of 3 years ending one month before the day on
-- which the non-use application is filed, and, at no time during that period, the person who was then the registered owner:
-- (i) used the trade mark in Australia; or (ii) used the trade mark in good faith in Australia". s 93(2): that ground "may only
-- be made after a period of 3 years beginning from the date the particulars of the trade mark were entered into the Register".
-- s 7(3): an authorised use is use by the owner. s 100(1), (3): in an opposed application it is for me, the owner opposing, to
-- rebut the allegation, by showing use in good faith or (3)(c) "circumstances ... that were an obstacle to the use".
-- s 101(3): "If satisfied that it is reasonable to do so, the Registrar or the court may decide that the trade mark should not
-- be removed from the Register even if the grounds ... have been established."

DECLARE NonUseFacts HAS
    `the day the non-use application is filed` IS A NUMBER
    `I had a good-faith intention to use it in Australia when I filed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I or an authorised user used it in good faith in Australia before the last month` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I or an authorised user used it in good faith in Australia in the 3 years ending one month before` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an obstacle prevented use in that period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Registrar or court thinks it reasonable not to remove it` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE NonUse IS ONE OF
    `it may be removed (s 92(4)(a)): no good-faith intention at filing and no use`
    `it may be removed (s 92(4)(b)): 3 years without use`
    `not removed: the Registrar or court thinks it reasonable to keep it (s 101(3))`
    `not removed: an obstacle prevented use (s 100(3)(c))`
    `not removed: I used it, or the 3-year ground is not yet open (ss 92(4)(b), 93(2))`

-- INFERENCE: "registered for a continuous period of 3 years ending one month before" the application day is tested as: the date
-- of registration, plus 37 months under s 6A, falls on or before that day.
GIVEN `my registration` IS A Registration @desc Your registration
      `the facts` IS A NonUseFacts @desc The non-use application and your use
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 3-year ground is open` IF
        `the day a period of months ends` (`my registration`'s `date particulars were entered in the Register`) 36 AT MOST `the facts`'s `the day the non-use application is filed`
    AND `the day a period of months ends` (`When does my registration take effect` `my registration`) 37 AT MOST `the facts`'s `the day the non-use application is filed`

@export Can my trade mark be removed from the Register for non-use (ss 92, 93, 100, 101)?
GIVEN `my registration` IS A Registration @desc Your registration
      `the facts` IS A NonUseFacts @desc The non-use application and your use
GIVETH A NonUse
DECIDE `Can my mark be removed for non-use` IS
    BRANCH IF `ground (a)` AND `the facts`'s `the Registrar or court thinks it reasonable not to remove it`
              THEN `not removed: the Registrar or court thinks it reasonable to keep it (s 101(3))`
           IF `ground (a)` THEN `it may be removed (s 92(4)(a)): no good-faith intention at filing and no use`
           IF `ground (b) unanswered by use` AND `the facts`'s `an obstacle prevented use in that period`
              THEN `not removed: an obstacle prevented use (s 100(3)(c))`
           IF `ground (b) unanswered by use` AND `the facts`'s `the Registrar or court thinks it reasonable not to remove it`
              THEN `not removed: the Registrar or court thinks it reasonable to keep it (s 101(3))`
           IF `ground (b) unanswered by use` THEN `it may be removed (s 92(4)(b)): 3 years without use`
           OTHERWISE `not removed: I used it, or the 3-year ground is not yet open (ss 92(4)(b), 93(2))`
    WHERE
        `ground (a)` MEANS
                (NOT `the facts`'s `I had a good-faith intention to use it in Australia when I filed`)
            AND (NOT `the facts`'s `I or an authorised user used it in good faith in Australia before the last month`)
            AND `the facts`'s `the day the non-use application is filed` GREATER THAN `my registration`'s `filing date`
        `ground (b) unanswered by use` MEANS
                `the 3-year ground is open` `my registration` `the facts`
            AND (NOT `the facts`'s `I or an authorised user used it in good faith in Australia in the 3 years ending one month before`)

§§ `s 151 -- marking it as registered`

-- s 151(1): "A person must not make a representation to the effect that a trade mark is a registered trade mark unless the
-- person knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that the trade mark is registered in Australia. Penalty: 60 penalty
-- units." (3): the same for a representation that it is registered "in respect of goods or services". (5): use of "the word
-- registered" or "any other word or any symbol referring ... to registration" is such a representation (with exceptions for
-- foreign registrations, not encoded).
@export May I mark my trade mark as registered (for example with the symbol for a registered mark) on these goods or services on this day (s 151)?
GIVEN `my registration` IS A Registration @desc Your registration
      `the day` IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the marking, YYYYMMDD
      `the goods or services are within my registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the goods or services marked are ones the mark is registered for
      `I otherwise have reasonable grounds to believe it is registered for them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have reasonable grounds to believe it is registered in Australia for them
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I mark it as registered` IF
        (    `my registration`'s `date particulars were entered in the Register` GREATER THAN 0
         AND `the day` AT LEAST `my registration`'s `date particulars were entered in the Register`
         AND `the day` LESS THAN `When does my registration now expire` `my registration`
         AND `the goods or services are within my registration`)
    OR  `I otherwise have reasonable grounds to believe it is registered for them`

@export What is the most I can be fined for falsely marking a trade mark as registered, in penalty units (s 151)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for a false representation in penalty units` IS 60
